e] [17592186365958 1145 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,0) & =\\frac{2(-1)}{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2(0)}{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}\\,j \\\\  & =(-1)i+0\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,0)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-0⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365960 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365961 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365962 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365963 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365964 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1041 "selection" 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365961 13194139535781 true] [17592186365959 1110 #uuid "2f51af24-b51a-5d2e-abb6-cb06cae2df23" 13194139535781 true] [17592186365960 1034 "⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186365960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186365960 1111 #uuid "72f2a4bb-cebc-55e1-9a75-437026044a5b" 13194139535781 true] [17592186365961 1034 "⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186365961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [175