ne to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,2).$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366007 1113 #uuid "7975c9aa-052b-5a25-9627-4a7d8aff7ed9" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366007 1145 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy)\\,j \\\\  & =(2x{y}^{2}+y)\\,i+(2y{x}^{2}+x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2) & =(2(1)(2)^{2}+(2))\\,i+(2(2)(1)^{2}+(1))\\,j \\\\  & =10\\,i+5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨10,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨10,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366009 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366010 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366011 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366012 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366013 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1041 "selection" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366011 13194139535781 true] [17592186366008 1110 #uuid "096cf923-1846-56b4-9079-05fc47b71dc5" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366009 1034 "⟨8,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366009 1111 #uuid "15067bac-5f50-5a66-9f78-d960be749231" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366010 1034 "⟨15,10⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" 131941395