},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366016 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366017 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366018 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366019 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366020 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1041 "selection" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366020 13194139535781 true] [17592186366015 1110 #uuid "1dd633ae-c063-5e27-a4cc-b4f697474c1e" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366016 1034 "⟨3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366016 1111 #uuid "0b19fa08-b3d4-58bf-8b6a-6d0a921a167c" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366017 1034 "⟨4,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366017 1111 #uuid "5bb58c24-f9de-5884-864d-bda87a6da32b" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366018 1034 "⟨-5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366018 1111 #uuid "bb86f54d-3dfc-5df7-acc6-5c7099191532" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366019 1034 "⟨2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366019 1111 #uuid "84e85b34-e2ca-50b0-b18f-081553e7f467" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366020 1034 "⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366020 1111 #uuid "e1dc6ab9-cfb6-5369-8e57-51391b3bb68e" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366021 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366022 13194139535781 true] [17592186366021 1089 "q-72400" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366021 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535781 true] [17592186366021 1100 "Consider the plane curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2xy+9.$ Find a tangent vector to that curve at the point $(-1,2).$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366021 1113 #uuid "96e37626-e43e-531a-94f2-e33ce2598b5e" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366021 1145 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2xy+9 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy-9$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-1,2)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(-1,2)={f}_{y}(-1,2)\\,i-{f}_{x}(-1,2)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy-9)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy-9)\\,j \\\\  & =(2y-2x)\\,i-(2x-2y)\\,j \\\\ t(-1,2) & =(2(2)-2(-1))\\,i-(2(-1)-2(2))\\,j \\\\  & =6\\,i+6\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $6\\,i+6\\,j.$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366023 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366024 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366025 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366026 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366027 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1041 "selection" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366024 13194139535781 true] [17592186366022 1110 #uuid "4ed1e1e0-70f1-5784-bb56-8cad9427026d" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366023 1034 "i-j" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366023 1111 #uuid "4d701a25-9b1d-59e1-87c6-edee8a104153" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366024 1034 "6\\,i+6\\,j" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366024 1111 #uuid "b43bbefb-fb27-5318-b9f1-b71cbba3cb66" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366025 1034 "i+6\\,j" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366025 1111 #uuid "e28ecaba-deab-587e-a644-9bf0c621da2d" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366026 1034 "2\\,i-j" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366026 1111 #uuid "b2582f4b-c1cd-53d0-806d-fe3486746ac5" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366027 1034 "2\\,i-6\\,j" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535781 true] [17592186366027 1111 #uuid "8fbdaf61-e1c9-57f0-b895-ab7d36ec509f" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366028 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366029 13194139535781 true] [17592186366028 1089 "q-72410" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366028 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535781 true] [17592186366028 1100 "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}+2xy={x}^{2}+8$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j?$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366028 1113 #uuid "5d4b6633-13b7-5d79-8080-f17cf9d74729" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366028 1145 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2xy & ={x}^{2}+8 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=8.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2})i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2})j \\\\  & =2(y+x)\\,i-2(y-x)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ (2(y+x)\\,i-2(y-x)\\,j)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ -2(y-x) & =0 \\\\ y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=x$ into the equation of our curve gives:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ (x)^{2}+2x(x)-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $x=2$, we get $y=2$ and the corresponding point is $(2,2).$\n\n- If $x=-2$, we get $y=-2$ and the corresponding point is $(-2,-2).$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366030 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366031 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366032 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366033 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366034 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1041 "selection" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366031 13194139535781 true] [17592186366029 1110 #uuid "03179b55-c711-5e80-80a8-9df2a2adf187" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366030 1034 "$(0,2)$ and $(1,2)$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366030 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535781 true] [17592186366030 1111 #uuid "ebc980b5-b7aa-5431-9aa2-b29be3a530b8" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366031 1034 "$(2,2)$ and $(-2,-2)$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535781 true] [17592186366031 1111 #uuid "ba79566f-77e7-5fa4-bad8-c38119bf080e" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366032 1034 "$(2,0)$  and $(0,2)$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535781 true] [17592186366032 1111 #uuid "56595132-b849-588a-aa5a-42a19c3c9886" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366033 1034 "$(0,2)$ only" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535781 true] [17592186366033 1111 #uuid "edc63ae4-4757-5727-b3cb-80691563851b" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366034 1034 "$(1,2)$ and $(2,1)$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535781 true] [17592186366034 1111 #uuid "bbe198f9-7bb5-5597-a520-88af09679064" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366035 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366036 13194139535781 true] [17592186366035 1089 "q-72412" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366035 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535781 true] [17592186366035 1100 "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}-4xy=-5{x}^{2}+1$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366035 1113 #uuid "49dc4b38-854b-53b5-ba44-1bf47c27ef1c" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366035 1145 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4xy & =-5{x}^{2}+1 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=1.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2})i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2})j \\\\  & =2(y-2x)\\,i-(10x-4y)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $i$, we must have $t\\cdot i=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ (2(y-2x)\\,i-(10x-4y)\\,j)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ 2(y-2x) & =0 \\\\ y & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=2x$ into the equation of our curve gives:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (2x)^{2}-4x(2x)+5{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8{x}^{2}+5{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $x=1$, we get $y=2$ and the corresponding point is $(1,2).$\n\n- If $x=-1$, we get $y=-2$ and the corresponding point is $(-1,-2).$" 13194139535781 true] [17592186366036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366037 13194139535781 true] [17592186366036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366038 13194139535781 true] [175921863